WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.594 --> 00:00:03.693
- [Interviewee] My mum is Danette Burse;

00:00:03.693 --> 00:00:06.862
an incredible and gentle spirit

00:00:06.862 --> 00:00:09.898
who taught me everything I know.

00:00:09.898 --> 00:00:13.525
That's who my mum is.
(somber music)

00:00:13.525 --> 00:00:16.020
- My mum is Doriane E. Miller.

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:20.540
- My mum is Marilyn Dresler.

00:00:20.547 --> 00:00:23.580
- My mum is Kristian Gilmore Pine.

00:00:23.592 --> 00:00:25.037
- You know I feel like
there's not too many people

00:00:25.037 --> 00:00:26.996
you come across in the world that like,

00:00:26.996 --> 00:00:29.989
every moment you have
together is just like

00:00:29.989 --> 00:00:31.524
intrinsically beautiful.

00:00:31.524 --> 00:00:34.288
- She is an amazing woman.

00:00:34.288 --> 00:00:37.121
The most stubborn, strongest woman

00:00:38.401 --> 00:00:39.403
I've ever met.

00:00:39.403 --> 00:00:40.325
- She really pushed me,

00:00:40.325 --> 00:00:43.542
she really motivated me
to do all these things,

00:00:43.542 --> 00:00:44.436
she helped me.

00:00:44.436 --> 00:00:46.722
- She can make everybody
her friend kind of

00:00:46.722 --> 00:00:48.597
and I think that's something
that she gave to me.

00:00:48.597 --> 00:00:50.049
- I know a lot of people
like in this world

00:00:50.049 --> 00:00:51.779
like they hold grudges.

00:00:51.779 --> 00:00:55.196
She had an incredible ability to forgive.

00:00:59.298 --> 00:01:01.145
- My mother died of pneumonia.

00:01:01.145 --> 00:01:02.826
Remember seeing my father
cry for the first time

00:01:02.826 --> 00:01:05.458
but other than that I
don't really remember much

00:01:05.458 --> 00:01:06.956
outside of home videos.

00:01:06.956 --> 00:01:11.567
- My mom got really sick
when I was really young.

00:01:11.567 --> 00:01:13.608
- They missed a lump in one of her breasts

00:01:13.608 --> 00:01:15.657
and the lump spread
through her second breast;

00:01:15.657 --> 00:01:18.069
hair, lymph nodes,
stomach, back, and brain,

00:01:18.069 --> 00:01:20.905
and they only gave her six weeks to live,

00:01:20.905 --> 00:01:22.605
and I was a sophomore in
high school at the time.

00:01:22.605 --> 00:01:26.156
- My mom was diagnosed with
a rare form of breast cancer

00:01:26.156 --> 00:01:29.573
and in September of 2014 she passed away.

00:01:30.561 --> 00:01:33.474
- I didn't really know how
cancer was going to work.

00:01:33.474 --> 00:01:36.633
I didn't know how quickly it would act.

00:01:36.633 --> 00:01:38.633
- She passed on May 1st.

00:01:39.993 --> 00:01:41.576
We buried her May 3rd.

00:01:41.576 --> 00:01:43.361
My birthday is May 5th.

00:01:43.361 --> 00:01:46.058
I graduated on Mother's Day May 9th.

00:01:46.058 --> 00:01:50.141
- It's one thing to like
lose a parent, you know.

00:01:51.283 --> 00:01:55.046
It's also like another
thing to lose a best friend.

00:01:55.046 --> 00:01:56.723
I think that it's not something

00:01:56.723 --> 00:01:59.640
you ever really get over, you know?

00:02:00.850 --> 00:02:04.637
You just learn to
understand what it means.

00:02:04.637 --> 00:02:06.760
I just learned to love harder.

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:10.404
- I lived in fear for many,
many years of my life.

00:02:10.404 --> 00:02:11.731
She was sick for eight years

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:13.405
before she finally passed away.

00:02:13.405 --> 00:02:15.131
Every morning I would go to school,

00:02:15.131 --> 00:02:18.831
not sure if she'd be
there when I got home.

00:02:18.831 --> 00:02:19.848
- She was such a good person

00:02:19.848 --> 00:02:23.355
that would listen and just give eloquent,

00:02:23.355 --> 00:02:25.712
and intelligent, and thoughtful responses,

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:27.383
and caring responses.

00:02:27.383 --> 00:02:29.647
- I used to have to like do
those science fair projects

00:02:29.647 --> 00:02:31.880
that everybody has to do
with like the poster board

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:33.152
and everything like that,

00:02:33.152 --> 00:02:35.580
and my mom would like get more excited

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:37.628
about the project than I would.

00:02:37.628 --> 00:02:40.038
So like, I would stay up all night long,

00:02:40.038 --> 00:02:41.066
putting together what I thought

00:02:41.066 --> 00:02:42.494
was an incredible project,

00:02:42.494 --> 00:02:45.152
and I would wake up and
like the poster board

00:02:45.152 --> 00:02:47.207
would be completely different.

00:02:47.207 --> 00:02:49.610
It would be like cut-out
and like trekked down,

00:02:49.610 --> 00:02:52.239
they'll be like 3D and all of this stuff,

00:02:52.239 --> 00:02:53.452
and we would just have this moment

00:02:53.452 --> 00:02:55.425
where I would just like look at her

00:02:55.425 --> 00:02:56.468
and she'll look at me.

00:02:56.468 --> 00:02:59.681
And I remember coming home
with the first place medal

00:02:59.681 --> 00:03:02.514
and I was just like Mom we did it!

00:03:04.308 --> 00:03:06.828
And she was like, "Yeah, we did that."

00:03:06.828 --> 00:03:10.578
- The day after she had
this brain operation,

00:03:11.582 --> 00:03:13.702
I wrote this paper and it was garbage.

00:03:13.702 --> 00:03:16.498
And she took it and she
revamped the whole thing,

00:03:16.498 --> 00:03:18.097
and when I got it I was like,

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:19.132
this doesn't even sound like I wrote this,

00:03:19.132 --> 00:03:19.965
I don't know if I can submit this.

00:03:19.965 --> 00:03:22.211
She was like, "You'll be
fine. Just submit it."

00:03:22.211 --> 00:03:25.591
And I got the paper back the next day

00:03:25.591 --> 00:03:27.813
and I got a B plus,

00:03:27.813 --> 00:03:31.522
and she was so pissed
because she didn't get an A,

00:03:31.522 --> 00:03:33.946
and that's the type of person she was.

00:03:33.946 --> 00:03:37.159
- As I grow older and realize more

00:03:37.159 --> 00:03:39.359
how my mom kept it together for us

00:03:39.359 --> 00:03:42.380
and how long she fought to stay alive

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:44.119
to be around for her children,

00:03:44.119 --> 00:03:46.217
that's who my mom is.

00:03:46.217 --> 00:03:48.056
- I find myself talking to my mom

00:03:48.056 --> 00:03:49.960
at least once or twice a day.

00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:51.063
- Certain times I talk less,

00:03:51.063 --> 00:03:52.518
sometimes we talk more.

00:03:52.518 --> 00:03:53.601
You know it really depends on

00:03:53.601 --> 00:03:56.548
how bad of a day I'm having.

00:03:56.548 --> 00:03:59.425
- I say hi to her everyday.

00:03:59.425 --> 00:04:01.575
Sometimes out loud, sometimes not.

00:04:01.575 --> 00:04:05.360
- I felt like intrinsically
like she became my argonaut,

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:08.913
like she gave her life
to be a protector for me.

00:04:08.913 --> 00:04:12.886
And so I got this tattoo that says argo

00:04:12.886 --> 00:04:15.552
and I got it at all lowercase

00:04:15.552 --> 00:04:18.290
because she was an
extremely humble person,

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:20.968
but I got it in bold because
her presence was felt

00:04:20.968 --> 00:04:22.052
wherever she went,

00:04:22.052 --> 00:04:23.458
and I got it on my foreman

00:04:23.458 --> 00:04:25.945
because I wanted to wear
her bravery on my sleeve.

00:04:25.945 --> 00:04:28.165
- Mom, I just want to say I love you

00:04:28.165 --> 00:04:30.342
and thank you for everything
you've instilled in me.

00:04:30.342 --> 00:04:32.194
- Even though she's not physically here,

00:04:32.194 --> 00:04:34.552
my mom is still very much a part of me

00:04:34.552 --> 00:04:36.727
and who I am everyday.

00:04:36.727 --> 00:04:39.436
- Thank you for everything.

00:04:39.436 --> 00:04:40.659
Thank you for your sacrifices

00:04:40.659 --> 00:04:45.426
and everything you did for
me, for Seth, for Emmett.

00:04:45.426 --> 00:04:47.102
I hope we've made you proud.

00:04:47.102 --> 00:04:49.489
Everything that we've
done is because of you.

00:04:49.489 --> 00:04:50.450
Everything we've wanted to do,

00:04:50.450 --> 00:04:53.217
everything we've driven
for is because of you.

00:04:53.217 --> 00:04:56.870
- Mom I love you so much
and I miss you everyday,

00:04:56.870 --> 00:04:58.812
and I still think about you everyday.

00:04:58.812 --> 00:05:02.590
Even though I only had it
for a limited amount of time,

00:05:02.590 --> 00:05:03.840
I feel so lucky

00:05:05.298 --> 00:05:08.659
to have the bond that
I did with my mother.

00:05:08.659 --> 00:05:10.996
- We used to have this thing where like

00:05:10.996 --> 00:05:13.246
we would never say goodbye.

00:05:14.316 --> 00:05:15.983
So it's not goodbye.

00:05:17.372 --> 00:05:19.289
It's just see you later

00:05:20.285 --> 00:05:21.118
and

00:05:23.269 --> 00:05:24.102
I'm okay.

00:05:27.362 --> 00:05:28.279
We're okay.

00:05:30.889 --> 00:05:31.889
I love you.

